abstract: >-
  We establish three algebraic and analytic identities relating shifted Hermite-Biehler
  kernels, critical-line multiplicity jets, and holomorphic prime-power multipliers to
  the transverse Wronskian W(d,t) = (1/2) d_d |Xi(t-id)|^2 of Riemann's Xi-function,
  together with explicit circularity and domain obstructions. First, for E_alpha(z) =
  Xi(z) - i*alpha*Xi'(z), the diagonal Nevanlinna-Pick kernel satisfies K_alpha(t-id,
  t-id) = (alpha/pi)*W_tilde(d,t) unconditionally, while positive semidefiniteness of
  the associated Cauchy-Pick matrices is equivalent to the Riemann Hypothesis (Levinson
  1974, Lagarias 2005/2006). Second, at an order-m real zero of a real-entire function f,
  the Jensen-Laguerre transverse coefficients satisfy c_1 = ... = c_{2m-3} = 0 and
  c_{2m-1}(t_0) = [m/(m!)^2]*(f^{(m)}(t_0))^2 > 0, inducing a local quadratic bowl whose
  definite vs. indefinite sign distinguishes real Lehmer pairs from off-critical conjugate
  zeros. Third, we prove the cross-term-free Leibniz-Wronskian identity for holomorphic
  multipliers, establish 0 <= b_n^E(X) <= 1 for truncated exponential Euler factors on
  Re(s) > 1, and document the Schwarz-reflection, functional-equation, and strip-residue
  obstructions that prevent unconditional off-line positivity.
